// @name: Sample kit — basic (leak test)
// @tagline: `new sample kick_909` / `new sample hat_909` — DEPENDS on the Mercury sample set
// @description: Verbatim from the mercury-engine README "Evaluate a mercury code file" usage
//   snippet. `kick_909`/`hat_909` are NOT bundled inside the mercury-engine npm package — the
//   engine's constructor eagerly fetches its ~200-entry default sample map from
//   raw.githubusercontent.com/tmhglnd/mercury-playground (confirmed by reading
//   node_modules/mercury-engine/dist/mercury.js: `this.baseUrl = this.samples['_base']` then
//   `new Tone.ToneAudioBuffers({ urls: this.samples, ... })`). If that fetch is blocked, slow, or
//   still in flight when this patch is evaluated, `kick_909`/`hat_909` play SILENTLY — no error
//   is thrown (mercury-engine issue #1, open: "Fix sample loading await before evaluation").
//   Explicit leak test: this file is the control that should sound identical to the reference
//   player, and won't if the sample fetch failed or lost the race.
// @language: mercury
// @outputs: audio
// @level: didactic
// @tags: mercury, ab-corpus, sample, leak-test, sample-set
// @source: https://github.com/tmhglnd/mercury-engine/blob/main/README.md#resume-evaluate-and-silence
//
// A/B — mercury — Sample kit (leak test). Original: https://github.com/tmhglnd/mercury-engine/blob/main/README.md
// Coller/évaluer la voix, puis comparer au rendu de l'outil original (mercury.timohoogland.com).
// Test de fuite : dépend du jeu de samples distant (raw.githubusercontent.com) — silence si non chargé.

@core
@tempo:120

@actor v  eval.mercury

S -> v

v -> `new sample kick_909 time(1/4)
new sample hat_909 time(1/4 1/8) gain(0.6)`:4
